{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '64,135p'; rg -n '\"'^(class|def|    def) '\"' paid_gate.py; cat rehearsal.log; cat paid-mutants.log\"","aggregated_output":"    64\t  - each passage exactly as the request showed it, including those named only in `rests_on`;\n    65\t  - declared figures with renumbered ids, the recomputed outcomes and the recorded assumptions;\n    66\t  - the cards a non-reconciled separate unit has;\n    67\t  - neutral decision labels.\n    68\t- **Rehearsal:** 27 of 27 (`rehearsal.log`). The $0 gate still passes (`gate-run27.txt`: 87 of 87), and the mutants are unchanged.\n    69\t\n    70\t## 3c. After council round 47b (`codex-r47b.md`)\n    71\t\n    72\t- **[47b.1] Reconciliation:**\n    73\t  - Two recomputed values are the same when their bounds match and each end agrees within 1e-9 relative. A floating-point copy\n    74\t    unifies; a real difference stays a conflict.\n    75\t  - The readers never see the unified calculation. Each card of a reconciled packet is shown with its own original answer.\n    76\t- **[47b.2] Completeness comes from the attempt records.** `answers.jsonl` is the one record of what happened. For each planned unit\n    77\t  and draw, the final status is derived from it:\n    78\t  - no started line: **not sent**;\n    79\t  - a started line with no finished line: **interrupted**;\n    80\t  - a first refusal with no retry sent: **retry not sent**;\n    81\t  - otherwise, the last attempt's decision, and a second refusal is **unresolved**.\n    82\t\n    83\t  `results.json` is written from these records in a `finally`, so an abort still leaves it. The verdict is INCOMPLETE for every\n    84\t  status other than published, held or unresolved. That includes a reservation or HTTP failure, recorded as **transport**.\n    85\t- **[47b.3] Packets:**\n    86\t  - Every attempt of every card is listed, with neutral labels and check codes only.\n    87\t  - Each card is its own derivation: the figures its outcome and reference rest on, renumbered F1.. for that card alone.\n    88\t  - Its recorded assumptions are mapped to the same numbers. A record that names a figure outside the card is left out.\n    89\t- **[47b.4] Binding:**\n    90\t  - `packets.md` and the key are each created exclusively, once. A second `packets` call is refused.\n    91\t  - The key carries the run's digest (`answers.jsonl`, `results.json`, `plan.json`) and the sha256 of `packets.md`.\n    92\t  - The readings file carries the sha256 of the packets it was read on.\n    93\t  - The verdict is INCOMPLETE when any of the three differs, or when a ground is not a non-empty string naming a passage (e…) or a\n    94\t    figure (F…) of that packet.\n    95\t- **Rehearsal:** 41 of 41 (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n    96\t  - a floating-point copy unifies;\n    97\t  - a reconciled card shows its own derivation;\n    98\t  - every attempt is listed;\n    99\t  - a transport failure makes the verdict INCOMPLETE;\n   100\t  - an interruption during a retry leaves results, marks the unit interrupted and the rest not sent;\n   101\t  - a retry that was never sent is incomplete;\n   102\t  - the card view maps assumption records and leaves out other cards';\n   103\t  - a second packets run, readings made on other packets, a run changed after freezing, and null or foreign grounds are each refused\n   104\t    or INCOMPLETE.\n   105\t- **Mutants:** 13 of 13 caught, and the control passes (`paid_mutants.py`, `paid-mutants.log`). Each mutant breaks one of these\n   106\t  defences on a scratch copy. The plan is unchanged (sha256 `6f81dae5…`), and `calc_check.py` is unchanged since gate run 27.\n   107\t\n   108\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   109\t\n   110\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   111\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   112\t  - Each packet shows the questions, every passage a figure or citation names (as the request showed it), the figures and the cards.\n   113\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. Its cards cannot count as usable.\n   114\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   115\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   116\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   117\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   118\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   119\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   120\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   121\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   122\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines):\n   123\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   124\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   125\t    singleton answers.\n   126\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   127\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   128\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   129\t\n   130\t## 5. What the result decides\n   131\t\n   132\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   133\t  step Alex opens.\n   134\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n45:def W(population, measure, scope, period):\n49:def bands(draw, view_id):\n55:def passages(draw, evidence_ids):\n63:def pair_family(draw, total, dc):\n71:def only(family, view_id):\n75:def questions(draw, view_ids):\n85:def shown_lines(user):\n95:def item(unit, arm, draw, calls, family, shown):\n103:def build_plan():\n117:def plan(out):\n136:def strip(data):\n140:class Gate:\n141:    def __init__(self, out, transport, ledger=None):\n147:    def request(self, it, user):\n150:    def record(self, line):\n154:    def attempt(self, it, draw, user, n):\n181:    def unit(self, it, draw):\n190:    def run(self, items):\n202:def attempt_records(out):\n207:def derive_finals(out, items):\n233:def summarise(out, items, ledger_state):\n253:def _same_value(a, b):\n260:def merge(parts):\n327:def budget_module():\n335:def send(out, approved, plan_path):\n376:def normalise(calc):\n402:def run_digest(out):\n410:def card_view(calc, view_id, recorded):\n432:def packets(out, key_dir):\n498:def _grounded(ground, grounds):\n503:def final_readings(pid, cards, members, grounds=()):\n526:def verdict(out, readings_path, key_dir):\nPASS  clean: 36 first attempts, no retry  36 attempts\nPASS  clean: every body byte-equal to the planned request  []\nPASS  clean: every unit publishes  \nPASS  clean: the separate arm reconciles in all 9 pairs  \nPASS  clean: spend settled under the ceiling  spent 0.1156\nPASS  packets: 27 packets; no arm word or member prefix in the text  27 packets\nPASS  packets: the key is bound to the run and to the packet text  \nPASS  packets: a second packets run is refused, the key unchanged  /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b600\nPASS  verdict: both arms usable everywhere: STOP (gain under 3)  \nPASS  verdict: joint 9, separate 5: PASS  5\nPASS  verdict: one published singleton defect: STOP  \nPASS  verdict: a defect in the separate arm alone does not stop  \nPASS  verdict: missing packet: INCOMPLETE  P01: not read\nPASS  verdict: invented card: INCOMPLETE  P01: cards ['v999'] are not the unit's ['v29']\nPASS  verdict: missing ground: INCOMPLETE  P01 v29 usable: reader A gave no yes/no with a ground from this packet\nPASS  verdict: disagreement, no third: INCOMPLETE  P01 v29 usable: the readers disagree and no third reading decides\nPASS  verdict: a disagreement decided by the third reader is complete  \nPASS  verdict: null ground: INCOMPLETE  P01 v29 usable: reader A gave no yes/no with a ground from this packet\nPASS  verdict: ground naming nothing in the packet: INCOMPLETE  P01 v29 usable: reader A gave no yes/no with a ground from this packet\nPASS  verdict: readings made on other packets: INCOMPLETE  the readings were not made on the frozen packets\nPASS  verdict: a run changed after the packets were frozen: INCOMPLETE  the packet key does not belong to this run\nPASS  card view: own figures only, renumbered; the assumption record mapped, the other card's left out  [{\"figures\": [{\"id\": \"F1\", \"kind\": \"source\", \"evidence\": \"e7\", \"rests_on\": []}, {\"id\": \"F2\", \"kind\": \"computed\", \"inputs\": [\"F1\", \"F1\"], \"rests_on\": []}], \"answ\nPASS  separate-agree: equal shared Q3 forecasts are unified, and the pair reconciles  []\nPASS  separate-disagree: different shared Q3 forecasts are refused (C4)  \nPASS  div-zero: recorded and refused (C2), then retried  ['refused', 'publish']\nPASS  reservation: a refused reservation never reaches the provider and is recorded  0 provider calls\nPASS  send refuses no ceiling named  the approved ceiling is None (Alex names it); refused\nPASS  send refuses a changed plan  the plan is not the reviewed one (sha256 differs); refused\nPASS  send refuses a used authorization  /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b600\nPASS  retry: a refused calculation is retried once with its errors and then publishes  ['refused', 'publish']\nPASS  unresolved: two refusals make the unit unresolved  \nPASS  format: a schema-invalid answer is refused, then retried  ['format invalid', 'answered']\nPASS  separate: two answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3)  refused\nPASS  ledger-stop: after the ledger stops, nothing more is sent  5 attempts, 31 not sent\nPASS  separate-agree-float: Q3 forecasts equal within floating-point error are unified, and the pair reconciles  []\nPASS  packets: a reconciled card is shown with its own original derivation, not the unified copy  P12\nPASS  packets: every attempt is listed with its check codes  P14\nPASS  one-transport: a request that fails in transport is final as transport, not published  \nPASS  verdict: a unit failed in transport makes the verdict INCOMPLETE  single-E|single|1: transport; P19 v41 usable: reader A gave no yes/no with a ground from this packet\nPASS  interrupt: results are written from the records; the unit in flight is interrupted, the rest not sent  {'pair-old-2|joint|1': 'publish', 'pair-old-2|joint|2': 'not sent', 'pair-old-2|joint|3': 'not sent'}\nPASS  a refused first answer whose retry was never sent is incomplete, not refused or not sent  \n41 of 41 checks pass\nPASS  00 control  41 of 41 checks pass\nCAUGHT  01 equivalence is exact equality  FAIL  separate-agree-float: Q3 forecasts equal within floating-point error are unified, and the pair reconcile\nCAUGHT  02 a transport failure counts as finished  FAIL  verdict: a unit failed in transport makes the verdict INCOMPLETE  P23 v41 usable: reader A gave no yes/n\nCAUGHT  03 an attempt in flight is not seen  FAIL  interrupt: results are written from the records; the unit in flight is interrupted, the rest not sent  {\nCAUGHT  04 results only on a clean exit  c